From 22992ce1f27d2effbffdcea5aa2d711e55a2e0be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:39:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0027: the verdict lands on the boot stick, not a photograph

A boots report comes back only as a photograph today, and the owner has no camera in
the loop. The boot stick is a plain FAT32 data partition, so macOS mounts it at
/Volumes/OPENCORE; the kext now writes navi48-report.txt there from its own kernel
thread: same headline as the screen, the takeover verdict and cause, kext/accelerator
facts, injected ids, and the TTL census. One file per boot, rewritten until the verdict
is final - an unarmed (0x73BF pair) boot keeps watching for a late announce, since only
an armed timeout and a positive announce are final. Host suite: 64 checks; the plant
harness catches 34/34 breaks.
